{
  "title": "functions.expression.WithExpression.Nullable_Array_of_functions.expression.WithExpression.agent.completions.message.AssistantToolCallExpression",
  "description": "A value that can be either a literal or an expression.\n\nThis allows Function definitions to mix static values with dynamic\nexpressions. During compilation, expressions are evaluated while\nliteral values pass through unchanged.\n\n# Example\n\nLiteral value:\n```json\n\"hello world\"\n```\n\nJMESPath expression:\n```json\n{\"$jmespath\": \"input.greeting\"}\n```\n\nStarlark expression:\n```json\n{\"$starlark\": \"input['greeting']\"}\n```",
  "anyOf": [
    {
      "description": "An expression (JMESPath or Starlark) to evaluate.",
      "$ref": "functions.expression.Expression"
    },
    {
      "description": "A literal value.",
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "functions.expression.WithExpression.agent.completions.message.AssistantToolCallExpression"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "title": "functions.expression.WithExpression.agent.completions.message.InputAudio",
  "description": "A value that can be either a literal or an expression.

This allows Function definitions to mix static values with dynamic
expressions. During compilation, expressions are evaluated while
literal values pass through unchanged.

# Example

Literal value:
```json
"hello world"
```

JMESPath expression:
```json
{"$jmespath": "input.greeting"}
```

Starlark expression:
```json
{"$starlark": "input['greeting']"}
```",
  "anyOf": [
    {
      "description": "An expression (JMESPath or Starlark) to evaluate.",
      "$ref": "functions.expression.Expression"
    },
    {
      "description": "A literal value.",
      "$ref": "agent.completions.message.InputAudio"
    }
  ]
}

